From ab88195ea75d92df33ae591994979fb5289b0e89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mms-it-ch <info@mms-it.ch>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:18:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] rtl: z/OS support for sysutils, classes, math and the
 other base units

- objpas: iterate over the resource string pointer lists on z/OS
  (FPC_RESSTR_PTRLIST, see the compiler change)
- baseunix/unix: z/OS mmap constants (from ostypes.inc), SeekDir/TellDir
  through the C library (DIR is opaque), no GetDomainName
- unxdeclh/oscdeclh: fpFlock through fcntl (no flock), fpfStatFS through
  fstatvfs, no futimens on z/OS
- initc: errno through __errno; errors: StrError through strerror (no
  sys_errlist)
- zos: struct statvfs (measured on z/OS), MAP_ANONYMOUS, ptypes.inc only
  included by the system unit, SignalToRunError is the default signal
  handler used by sysutils
- s390x: mathu.inc (fixed rounding/exception modes for now)

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Anthropic)
